You will compare one known error in a data agent's work against a ranked list of items produced by a reviewer. Your job is to decide whether any item in the list identifies this known error, and if so, which one.

An item identifies the known error only if both of these hold:
- It is about the same thing: the same table, and the same column, computation, filter, or join.
- It points to the same problem: what the item says is wrong, assumed, or missing is the same as what went wrong in the known error. It does not matter whether the item is phrased as an assumption the agent made ("the agent assumes ...") or as a problem in the work ("this does not match ..."); judge by meaning.

An item does not count if it only says that something may be wrong without saying what, such as "this column may be computed incorrectly". An item about the same column but a different problem does not count.

If more than one item identifies the error, report the highest-ranked one. If you are unsure, say so rather than guessing.

Return a JSON object with:
- "verdict": "match", "no_match", or "unsure".
- "rank": the position of the matching item (1 is the top), or null.
- "quote": the exact words from the matching item that show it identifies the error, or null.
- "reason": one short sentence.

=== Known error ===
Table: int_pendo__conversion_funnel_analysis
What the agent's work assumed: avg_30d_overall_conversion_rate 用全部历史日期求平均就行
What was actually required or true: 只平均今天往前 30 天以内（含）的日期

=== Reviewer's ranked list for this table ===
[
  {
    "rank": 1,
    "item": {
      "problem": "Feature and deep-interaction activity are inferred from generic events instead of reading the feature-event and page-event sources.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "FROM staging.stg_pendo__event GROUP BY 1,2,3",
      "source": "daily_events (union all) ... feature_event ... page_event",
      "reason": "Two required data sources are unused, changing the population and all funnel counts."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 2,
    "item": {
      "problem": "Page-view presence is conditioned on non-NULL page_id even though any generic event should establish the page-view presence flag.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "count(DISTINCT CASE WHEN page_id IS NOT NULL THEN visitor_id END)",
      "source": "Page views: from staging.stg_pendo__event as event_type=page_view",
      "reason": "This changes the denominator of page-to-feature and overall conversion rates."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 3,
    "item": {
      "problem": "The required visitor/day aggregation, entity counts, and interaction totals are omitted.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "WITH daily AS (SELECT account_id,app_id,... count(DISTINCT visitor_id) ...)",
      "source": "user_daily_funnel (per visitor_id, account_id, app_id, event_date)",
      "reason": "Without this stage the specified engagement and session-quality metrics cannot be computed."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 4,
    "item": {
      "problem": "Engagement, per-visitor averages, and session-quality rates are NULL placeholders.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "NULL::DOUBLE avg_engagement_score ... NULL::FLOAT high_quality_session_rate,NULL::FLOAT bounce_rate",
      "source": "Averages ... avg_engagement_score ... Quality rates ... high_quality_session_rate ... bounce_rate",
      "reason": "Several required business measures are never calculated for any row."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 5,
    "item": {
      "problem": "The purported 30-day averages actually average every historical daily row.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "avg(overall_conversion_rate) OVER(PARTITION BY account_id,app_id)",
      "source": "dates on or after 30 days before today",
      "reason": "Historical behavior replaces the required current-window cohort summary."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 6,
    "item": {
      "problem": "Conversion trend is always NULL instead of comparing the two specified date windows.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "NULL::DOUBLE conversion_rate_trend",
      "source": "average ... on or after 7 days before today minus ... from 30 to 7 days before today",
      "reason": "The requested directional signal is completely absent."
    }
  },
  {
    "rank": 7,
    "item": {
      "problem": "Funnel health and optimization recommendations are constants rather than threshold-based classifications.",
      "about": "requirement",
      "evidence_in_work": "'Poor' funnel_health_rating,'Focus on feature discovery and onboarding' optimization_recommendation",
      "source": "funnel_health_rating ... Excellent ... Good ... Fair ... Poor; optimization_recommendation (first matching rule)",
      "reason": "Every account receives the same assessment regardless of its metrics."
    }
  }
]
